Specifically:

  spec/openapi.json is a verbatim vendored copy of that project's OpenAPI
  document. spec/README.md records the upstream commit it came from.

  types.go, event.go, session_types.go and enums.go declare Go types and
  constants mirroring that document's schemas, and their doc comments reproduce
  the document's own schema and property descriptions.

These files were previously produced by a code generator. They are now written
by hand, which changes how they are maintained and not what they derive from:
the descriptions are still the upstream project's, so this attribution still
applies.

Attribution notices in the upstream project's NOTICE file that pertain to its
Python runtime dependencies are omitted here, as this Software contains no part
of them — Apache License 2.0 section 4(d) provides for excluding notices that do
not pertain to any part of a Derivative Work.
